{"cve": "CVE-2026-33324", "version": "N/A", "published": "2026-05-05T20:16:36.317", "lastModified": "2026-05-08T19:22:59.910", "description": "SQLBot is an intelligent Text-to-SQL system based on large language models and RAG. In versions 1.7.0 and earlier, the Text2SQL chat interface is vulnerable to prompt injection. The user-provided question parameter is directly concatenated into the LLM prompt without filtering or escaping, and the SQL extracted from the LLM response is executed against the database without validation or sanitization. An authenticated attacker can craft a malicious question to manipulate the LLM into generating and executing arbitrary SQL statements. When connected to a PostgreSQL data source, this can lead to remote code execution via COPY FROM PROGRAM. This issue has been fixed in version 1.7.1.", "cvssScore": 8.8, "cvsseSeverity": "HIGH", "CWE": ["707", "74", "89", "943"], "CAPEC": ["13", "84", "76", "72", "3", "135", "279", "676", "47", "109", "66", "80", "7", "45", "470", "278", "83", "250", "28", "79", "53", "10", "24", "42", "276", "9", "34", "277", "105", "52", "108", "64", "8", "67", "78", "267", "71", "6", "14", "110", "120", "51", "468", "273", "43", "101", "46"], "TECHNIQUES": [{"id": "1027", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1562.003", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1574.006", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1574.007", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}], "DEFEND": [{"id": "D3-FA", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "File Analysis", "artifact": "File"}, {"id": "D3-FIM", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "File Integrity Monitoring", "artifact": "File"}, {"id": "D3-DA", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "Dynamic Analysis", "artifact": "Executable File"}, {"id": "D3-EFA", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "Emulated File Analysis", "artifact": "Executable File"}, {"id": "D3-FEV", "tactic": "Evict", "technique": "File Eviction", "artifact": "File"}, {"id": "D3-DF", "tactic": "Deceive", "technique":